-------------
Status (3/08/2019)
-------------

The majority of GDAL functionality exposed by the C API is available, as well as much of the OGR API.
Most functionality is not covered by tests or benchmarks.


-------------
Nearmap Update (08/04/2024)
-------------

We have merged changes from : github.com/lukeroth/gdal in https://github.com/nearmap/gdal/pull/4.
These changes require GDAL 3.6+ now.
While not documented cleary in the source repository, it is mentioned in a [comment](https://github.com/lukeroth/gdal/blob/d4ff2229365e0206000207bc101f72b0ab2b2310/algorithms.go#L364):
> // SizeOfStructure: Added in GDAL 3.6 to detect potential ABI issues. Should be set to sizeof(GDALGridLinearOptions)

Note: GDAL is available in debian bookworm , but not in bullseye and older versions.


-------------
Nearmap Update (28/10/2026)
-------------

Changes in https://github.com/nearmap/gdal/pull/7 (APIPLAT-1133, APIPLAT-1134):

* Builds and is tested with GDAL 3.13.3 and Go 1.26. `DataType.Size` uses `GDALGetDataTypeSizeBits`,
  since `GDALGetDataTypeSize` is deprecated.
* Strings GDAL allocates for the caller are now freed with `CPLFree` after they are copied:
  the `SpatialReference.To*` exports, `Geometry.ToGML`/`ToGML_Ex`/`ToJSON`/`ToJSON_ex`, and `Info`.
  These leaked on every call.
* String lists GDAL allocates for the caller are freed with `CSLDestroy`: `VSIReadDirRecursive` and
  `Dataset.FileList`. Both return nil when GDAL returns no list (an empty or missing directory, a dataset
  with no files), where they used to dereference NULL and crash.
* `AngularUnits`, `LinearUnits`, `TargetLinearUnits` and `PrimeMeridian` no longer free the name they
  return. GDAL owns it, and freeing it aborted the process (lukeroth/gdal#83).

Who frees what: `OSRExportTo*`, `OGR_G_ExportTo*` and `GDALInfo` results with `CPLFree`;
`VSIReadDirRecursive` and `GDALGetFileList` results with `CSLDestroy`; names returned by `OSRGet*`
are owned by the spatial reference and are not freed.

Known remaining issues: `ToPCI` and `ToUSGS` panic on every call (lukeroth/gdal#118), and
`Feature.FieldAsIntegerList` reads GDAL's 32-bit integers as 64-bit ones (lukeroth/gdal#117).
